@1 = ~Escort across the border~
@2 = ~We decided to help Varun escape the clutches of corruption that is closing in on him in Athkatla. We will escort him to Nashkel once he is ready. He is going to wait for us at City Gates.~
@3 = ~We escorted Varun safely from Athkatla to Nashkel, helping him escape his debts and begin a new life farther north.~

// CotSC localisation batch 6: Government District and Varun/Jaheira CHAIN; original entries preserved.
@4 = ~Someone needs to overthrow whoever is responsible for those damn taxes. I have 4 starving children, how am I suppose to feed them. Damn cowled mages and their oppressive rule.~
@5 = ~So long, my friend. I have business with the government but I am not sure how to approach it.~
@6 = ~What do you need with them?~
@7 = ~I haven't paid my debts. And now I am not sure how to tackle this. I gave them my word, I'll pay in time. Said time was two nights ago, and now I have no backup plan.~
@8 = ~I'm sorry. I don't think I can help you.~
@9 = ~Thank you so much. I'll pack my things, and wait for you by the City Gates. Come and meet me whenever you're ready.~
@10 = ~I've taken all I could. You ready?~
@11 = ~Yes. Let's go.~
@12 = ~Not yet.~
@13 = ~Hold on. Something is wrong. We are surrounded!~
@14 = ~You all right? That was a close call.~
@15 = ~We should move. Let's go.~
@16 = ~Hold on a second. We'll just take a look around.~
@17 = ~Nashkel. Here we are. We officially crossed the border. I am so thankful for your help. Here, take this scroll as a reward. I have no need for it, nor do I know how to decipher it. I am forever grateful, my friend.~
@18 = ~Can't you be more respectful of personal space? I do not need to breathe the same air as you, filthy adventurers.~
@19 = ~No manners. Typical for a dwarf. I tire of your impertinence. Begone!~
@20 = ~Pardon me, but me and my wife are having a disciplinary conversation right now and you are making it rather hard to bear with your stench flying all around us.~
@21 = ~My sincere apologies, lord Firecam. I did not realise you're here too. Accept my deepest apology.~
@22 = ~I don't think we've met. My name is Lady Ophelia Falcon. It is an honour to meet you. Don't get displeased by my husband's attitude. He comes from wealth, and unfortunately wealth makes people arrogant.~
@23 = ~A charmer as always, Sir Firecam. I wish you and your companions a nice day.~
@24 = ~You heard about a Unicorn Grove? Apparently you can meet actual unicorns there. Sounds like a fairy tale, but it isn't.~
@25 = ~What's the problem! I am innocent! He attacked me first! I am a self-respecting hobgoblin and I deserve to be out of here!~
@26 = ~Athkatlan laws are intimidating, but taxes do serve a purpose. It maintains infrastructure, military defense, and bureaucracy. Corruption is the issue however, and penalties for abhorring the law are grave.~
@27 = ~I presume so. I've never been in debt before. Times are tough and my financial crisis isn't helping. Is there anything else you can say that could help my situation?~
@28 = ~Athkatla does not have welfare; it values coin above human life. Poor citizens who default on their debts or taxes often have to sell themselves into indentured servitude or rely entirely on begging in the streets, where they face constant harassment.~
@29 = ~If you wish to avoid that I'd recommend you a few options. Seeking religious sanctity being one. They offer shelter if things go wrong and you end up on the streets, however they are desperately underfunded. They cannot pay off a citizen's government debts or stop the tax collectors from seizing property.~
@30 = ~Option two is even more desperate. Moving out of the city. If you are completely broke and cannot pay the fee to leave, the guards will turn you away, trapping you inside the city or forcing you out into the lawless, unprotected slums right outside the walls, so you better keep that in mind. And even if you escape the city limits and settle down as a farmer in the countryside, you cannot escape the Amnian Revenue Board.~
@31 = ~The lands around Athkatla are divided into fiefdoms ruled by noble lords. These lords are required to send taxes back to the Council of Six, meaning their local tax collectors will eventually find your new home. Unless you leave Amn and travel north toward Baldur's Gate.~
@32 = ~I cannot afford the fee to leave Athkatla, let alone resources for travel. However... if you escort me to Nashkel, I'll find my way north. I have enough money to fund a caravan to Beregost. I can find work there. Please, would you be willing to escort me?~
@33 = ~We would.~
@34 = ~We don't have time, I'm afraid.~
@35 = ~Aye, ye scabby little lizard-whelp! I ain't takin' orders from a talkin' sewer-rat with a foul, unwashed maw! Scurry back to the dirt where ye and yer pathetic kind belong, before I split ye from chin to chuff!~
@36 = ~Watch your mouth, Lord Falcon. My family respect you on account of our past experiences but don't make me spread the word about how you talk to us.~
@37 = ~I accept. Have a nice day.~
@38 = ~We shall not be displeased. We've met plenty such people. It is good to see you again, Lady Falcon.~
@39 = ~I know a little about that. It's nice to meet someone who shares a bit of kindness and virtue while being a noble.~
